### Electron Version

37.2.1

### What operating system(s) are you using?

Ubuntu

### Operating System Version

20.04

### What arch are you using?

x64

### Last Known Working Electron version

36.0.0

### Does the issue also appear in Chromium / Google Chrome?

No

### Expected Behavior

When calling the showOpenDialog() method with the 'openDirectory' property set, it should allow the user to select a folder.

### Actual Behavior

The dialog is opened to allow user to select file instead of folder.

### Testcase Gist URL

_No response_

### Additional Information

Note that an exist bug is reported here https://github.com/electron/electron/issues/48217.

It is not possible to create a test case Gist using Electron Fiddle due to this issue itself. See the last few comments in the existing bug report.

To reproduce the issue, create an empty fiddle project and add these changes:

**In Main.js**
```Javascript
const { ipcMain, dialog } = require('electron')

ipcMain.on('show-open-dialog', (event, arg)=> {
  dialog.showOpenDialog(mainWindow, {
      properties: ['openDirectory'],
      title: 'Select Directory'
  }).then((result) => {
      if (!result.canceled) {
          // In Electron 37, this returns file paths instead of directory paths
          event.sender.send('open-dialog-paths-selected', result.filePaths)
      }
  });
})
```

**In preload.js**
```Javascript
const { ipcRenderer } = require('electron')
ipcRenderer.on('open-dialog-paths-selected', (event, arg)=> {
    alert(arg);
});
ipcRenderer.send('show-open-dialog');
```
